    "growth_divergence_warning": "All 3- and 5-year CAGRs are cycle artefacts: they run from the FY2021-22 lumber super-cycle peak (EBITDA margin 35-40%) to the FY2024-25 housing trough (17-18%). Equity CAGR (+1.5% 5yr) diverges by >30% from EPS (-15.9%) and revenue (-1.7%). The 10-year revenue CAGR is used as the growth anchor instead.",
    "notes": "Owner-FCF CAGRs are not meaningful: FY2025 owner FCF is ~-$6M (trough, post-interest), so any CAGR ending there is undefined. FY2022 owner FCF was ~$2.28B (OCF 2,832 - capex 521 - SBC 33). Per-share history is only comparable post-FY2016 (Plum Creek merger 510M -> 749M shares)."
